      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m Dr. ____. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S001",
      "patient_response": "Hi, Dr. ____. Um, well, what finally scared me into coming in is that I just keep making these really dumb technical mistakes at work that I absolutely know better than to make. I'm a camera operator and editor, mostly freelance. Which, by the way, the freelance market is so crazy lately. Ever since the strikes, everyone is just scrambling for gigs, and the rates are all over the place. My friend Sarah actually just had to move back to Ohio because she couldn't find enough work, which is wild because she's been out here for like five years and she's so talented. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, I'm making these rookie mistakes. Like, I'll label camera cards wrong, or I'll completely miss a timecode note. And directors can be so picky about timecodes—I worked with this one guy last month who wanted everything logged down to the frame, but he wouldn't even give me a proper script notes file, he just texted me voice memos! Who texts voice memos for edit notes? \n\nBut... right, the mistakes. Like, I'll export a whole client cut with the wrong lower-third graphic on the screen, even after I’ve literally just sat there and checked it. It's just really starting to freak me out.",
