    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever had a period of at least several days when you felt unusually energetic or ‘up’ compared with your normal self?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, unusually energetic or 'up'? No, not really. I mean, I'm always kind of on the go, but not like a specific period of being way more up than usual. I'm just consistently... busy. Especially when I'm on set. You have to be, right? You're lugging gear around, running cables, chasing the talent. \n\nActually, speaking of running cables, I was on this reality shoot a couple of months ago, and the sound guy—oh my god, this sound guy—he refused to tape down his XLR cables properly. He kept saying it was a \"fluid set\" and we needed to be mobile. But like, dude, it's a liability! I tripped over his cable right in the middle of a take, almost dropped my RED camera. Do you know how much a RED costs? It's like holding a luxury car in your hands. If I had dropped that, I would have had to sell an organ on the black market to pay for it. Which, honestly, I don't even know how people do that. Like, who is buying black market kidneys? How do you even transport them? Do they just put them in those little Coleman coolers you take to the beach? \n\nAnyway, sorry. No, I don't think I've ever had a period where I felt, like, unnaturally energetic or anything like that. Just my normal level of bouncing around.",
