      "doctor_question": "Have you had a period of at least two weeks when you felt depressed or down most of the day nearly every day?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Depressed or down? Um, no, not really. I mean, I get stressed out, obviously, especially when deadlines are tight or a director is being impossible, but I wouldn't say I've ever felt depressed for two weeks straight. \n\nI don't even know how people have the time to be depressed for two weeks, honestly. Like, who has that kind of schedule? If I took two weeks off to just feel sad, I'd lose all my clients. Freelance life is brutal that way. You're only as good as your last gig. Like, I did this one music video a few years ago for this indie band—they were trying way too hard to be the next Arctic Monkeys, you know? The lead singer insisted on wearing these vintage leather pants in the middle of July in the desert. We were shooting out in Joshua Tree. It was easily a hundred and ten degrees out there. I kept telling the producer, \"Hey, this guy is gonna pass out,\" and they just brushed me off. And what do you know, three hours in, he completely drops. Face first into a cactus. It was a whole ordeal. We had to call an ambulance, the shoot got shut down, and I still haven't gotten paid for the second half of that day. Which reminds me, I really need to follow up with their management company, but they keep changing their email addresses. It's so shady. \n\nBut yeah, no, I've never had a period where I was just down all day for weeks. Just the usual stress, you know?",
